webClaimRoute.detail:
TOKEN PATH: page.tsx:13-16, identical shape to reset's — `use(params)` then `<ClaimScreen token={token} />`.

PAGE-LOAD VALIDATION — this is the pattern LD-15 wants mirrored. ClaimScreen.tsx:82-102:
```tsx
  useEffect(() => {
    let cancelled = false;
    publicClient()
      .get("/invites/claim/{token}", { params: { path: { token } } })
      .then((state) => {
        if (cancelled) return;
        setClaimState(state);
        setUsername(state.usernamePreset ?? "");
        setDisplayName(state.displayNamePreset ?? "");
        setEmail(state.emailPreset ?? "");
        setPhase("ready");
      })
      .catch((err) => {
        if (cancelled) return;
        if (err instanceof LoombreApiError && err.status === 404) setPhase("invalid");
        else setPhase("load-error");
      });
    return () => {
      cancelled = true;
    };
  }, [token]);
```
ENDPOINT/SDK CALL: the typed SDK call `client.get("/invites/claim/{token}", { params: { path: { token } } })`, i.e. operationId `getClaimState`, registered at /Users/ozzy/App Development/Loombre/packages/sdk/src/generated/paths.ts:100 and typed at packages/sdk/src/generated/types.ts:58. Note the 404 branch discriminates on `err instanceof LoombreApiError` (:96) while the SUBMIT branch uses `isApiProblem(err)` (:149) — two different predicates in the same file.

PHASES (:56): `type Phase = "loading" | "invalid" | "load-error" | "ready" | "submitting" | "claimed-email-dropped";`. "loading" renders `<AuthScreen><p className={styles.bodyText}>Checking your invite…</p></AuthScreen>` (:164-170). "load-error" (:186-196) is deliberately DISTINCT from "invalid" — heading "Couldn't load this invite", body "Check your connection and try again.", secondary Button "Try again" → `window.location.reload()`. A non-404 must never be mistaken for a dead token.

CLIENT: module-level `publicClient()` at :65-68 — `resolvePublicServerUrl(getAuthStore().getSnapshot().serverUrl)` then `new LoombreClient({ baseUrl: serverUrl.replace(/\/$/, ""), getAccessToken: () => null })`.

SUBMIT-TIME 404 IS ALSO HANDLED (:148-154): a token consumed between the GET and the POST re-enters the SAME "invalid" phase — the page-load probe does not replace the submit-time guard, it precedes it. /reset must keep BOTH for the same reason.

TESTS: ClaimScreen.test.tsx spies on both `get` and `post`; :127-136 asserts the 404-on-load invalid screen, :138-146 asserts load-error is distinct, :194-209 asserts a 422 keeps the form, :211-223 asserts a 404 on submit routes to the same invalid screen.
